W("What was Macaulay's Minute of 1835 and what were its effects?", 3, "He argued a single shelf of a European library was worth all native literature, and wanted a class of Indians English in taste, opinions, morals and intellect (1). Traditional schools declined and English became a language of prestige (1). It created clerks cheaply for the administration and divided English-educated elites from the masses (1).", "M"),
